course: dictionary
lesson: 2916
title: Dragonfly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dragonfly is a large flying insect with a long thin body and two pairs of clear wings. Read the words around a new word to find its meaning. «A dragonfly has 6 legs and 4 wings, like many insects.» The words insects, legs and wings tell you what kind of creature it is.
explain: Clues can also come from places. «Insects ... leaving an empty skin like the dragonfly nymph's by the pond» tells you the young form lives by water, because it is found by the pond. Dragonflies are often seen near water, so the clue fits.
explain: Watch for capital letters. «NASA's Dragonfly, a drone-like rotorcraft due to launch around 2028» is a name for a machine, not an insect. The words drone and rotorcraft are your clue, so always check the words around a capital letter.
fact: A dragonfly is a large flying insect with a long thin body and two pairs of clear wings.
fact: Dragonflies have 6 legs and 4 wings, like many insects.
fact: Dragonflies are often seen near water.
fact: Young dragonflies, called nymphs, live in water.
fact: Dragonflies eat mosquitoes.
exercise: «A dragonfly has 6 legs and 4 wings, like many insects.» How many wings does a dragonfly have? | 2 | 6 | *4 | 8
exercise: Where are dragonflies often seen? | In the desert | Under the ground | In deep caves | *Near water
exercise: Which insect do dragonflies eat? | *Mosquitoes | Butterflies | Ants | Bees
test: «NASA's Dragonfly, a drone-like rotorcraft due to launch around 2028» What kind of thing is NASA's Dragonfly? | A pond | An insect | A frog | *A flying machine like a drone
test: The young dragonflies, called nymphs, live where? | On land in trees | Inside other insects | In the sky | *In water
exam: Which of these describes a dragonfly's body and wings? | A body covered in fur | A short fat body and one wing | *A long thin body and two pairs of clear wings | A round body and no wings
